  "what_this_shows": "Three Opal locations hold Bloomberg closes keyed by security and date: the G4 security_market store (14 objects, 5,696 close points over 656 security ids, dated 2026-09-29 to 2026-10-14) is the primary, and the ticker-keyed bbg/ and price_history_px_last prefixes hold 9,858 and 26,823 points. Of the 3,059 listed securities, 41 (8 never-priced, 29 gap) have a close in the primary, but the primary covers 0 of the 4,371 unpriced securities and 0 of the 15,973,399 unpriced holding-days, because its 11 dates never coincide with the 3,322 dates of the unpriced holding-days (2013-04-08 to 2026-06-22).",
  "not_established": [
    "Coverage through the ticker-keyed stores (bbg/ and price_history_px_last) is not measured: the issuer's script joins on CUSIP, and their keys are ticker labels with no CUSIP mapping in the tree.",
    "The primary's security_id is a 9-character CUSIP-shaped key for 87 of its 656 ids; the other 569 are other identifier shapes. The join is by exact string.",
    "The Yahoo price store (yahoo/global/silver/price_history/) holds Yahoo closes keyed by CUSIP; it is not a Bloomberg location and is not counted toward coverage.",
    "Two committed one-day history draws (history-2026-10-10.parquet and history-2026-10-11.parquet, 2,929 rows each, ticker-keyed) sit in git under org/tier2_senior, not on S3; they are not in the sparse worktree and were read with git show HEAD into scratch, not counted here.",
    "The OPTION-C request holds one listed security back (held_back, never drawn); it is in the listed set, as round 102 counted it, which gives 3,059.",
    "The listed set (3,059 / 2,354 never-priced / 515 gap) and the served classes (4,371 / 3,791 / 580 / 15,973,399) reproduce round 102's record in this run.",
    "No Bloomberg call, no queue draw, no vendor API and no write was made; AWS reads were list_objects_v2, parquet footers and the named columns."
